title: 'xcm-executor: price the end-of-message refund and stop buying back a refund holding cannot take'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The surplus refund the executor runs at the end of every message was never charged. It is
    now charged the weigher's weight of a `RefundSurplus`, kept out of the refund and counted in
    the weight used, but only when the trader refunds something. The charge is taken per weight
    dimension: a dimension whose surplus does not cover it is not refunded, and a surplus that
    covers it in no dimension is left as it was.

    The `refund_surplus` benchmark now pays with the asset of the new
    `pallet_xcm_benchmarks::generic::Config::worst_case_for_refund`, which defaults to the asset of
    `worst_case_for_trader`. A runtime whose trader swaps, such as one with
    `SwapFirstAssetTrader`, should return an asset the trader swaps, so the weight of
    `RefundSurplus` includes the swap back on refund. Asset Hub Westend does.

    A refund is no longer bought back from the trader when holding is at capacity. `RefundSurplus`
    now fails with `HoldingWouldOverflow` before asking the trader when holding is at capacity for
    the refund or the leftover `fees`, even when their assets are in holding, and leaves both to
    the end of the message. There, holding takes the refund and any leftover `fees` regardless of
    its capacity and is trapped for the claimer as usual. Before, the trader bought the refund back,
    or dropped it when the buy-back failed, as it always did for `TakeFirstAssetTrader`, and the
    leftover `fees` were dropped with the executor; both are now claimable.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    A message that leaves surplus weight without an explicit `RefundSurplus` is charged the
    weight of one `RefundSurplus` for the refund the executor makes on its behalf, so the refund
    is that much smaller, and no refund is made when the surplus does not cover it.
crates:
- name: staging-xcm-executor
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-xcm-benchmarks
  bump: minor
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
